Subject: [PATCH] derphttp: bound proxy node dials and expose typed regional rejection

Upstreamable transport API: actual all-node CONNECT rejection, scoped by
client identity, regional node definitions and subscription generation.
No log-driven cancellation or new connection identity. Caller owns cancellation.

--- a/derp/derphttp/derphttp_client.go
+++ b/derp/derphttp/derphttp_client.go
@@ -7,6 +7,16 @@
 // A server can implement DERP over HTTPS and even if the TLS connection
 // intercepted using a fake root CA, unless the interceptor knows how to
 // detect DERP packets, it will look like a web socket.
+//
+// Upstreamable proxy startup boundary: proxied node dialing has the same bounded
+// TCP/TLS/CONNECT lifetime as direct dialing. SubscribeProxyRejections reports
+// actual exhaustion only when all eligible regional nodes return non-200 CONNECT
+// responses. Timeouts and other transient errors keep their existing behavior.
+// Subscriptions match the client's public key, region ID and node definitions, not
+// logs. Probers are excluded. Each subscription is a generation captured when a
+// regional dial starts; unsubscribe invalidates that generation, including delayed
+// results. Subscribe before Ping and always unsubscribe on exit. Channels are
+// buffered, never closed, and carry only status codes. Consumers own cancellation.
 package derphttp
 
 import (
@@ -14,8 +24,10 @@
